## Grounding (binding)

- Every on-screen string must be QUOTED or TRIMMED from the manifest above —
  never invented, never paraphrased, never translated. A validator rejects
  any string that does not trace to a manifest line.
- The classic rejection: CONNECTIVE copy you compose yourself — a divider
  label like "One platform", a caption like "developers, agents, and code",
  a words line that paraphrases the page's claim. If you wrote it instead of
  copying it, it is wrong. When nothing fits, pick a SHORT manifest item
  (a button label, an h2) verbatim.
- Punctuation and emphasis marks may differ; the words may not.
- ui-scene captions ground against THE PAGE THAT SCENE SHOWS; every other
  scene grounds against any presented page.
- `*word*` inside a string marks the accent highlight.
- If your previous storyboard was rejected: DELETE each rejected string or
  replace it with a verbatim manifest item — never rephrase a rejected
  string into new unquoted copy.

## Output (JSON, no prose)

{
  "name": string | null,   // a short display name for this film; null if unsure
  "theme": {"canvas": "#RRGGBB", "ink": "#RRGGBB"} | null,  // null = default
  "scenes": [ ... ]        // 3..8 scenes, ordered
}

Scene types (discriminator `type`); every scene carries `seconds` (a duration
INTENT — the system assigns exact frames):

- {"type":"words","seconds":1.5..4,"dark":bool,"lines":[string]}  // 1..4 lines, each ≤30 chars
- {"type":"hero","seconds":2..5,"word":string,"sub":string}  // word ≤16 chars, sub ≤90
- {"type":"ui","seconds":3..10,"page":int,"focuses":[{"at":s,"x":0..1,"y":0..1,"zoom":1..4}],"captions":[{"at":s,"text":string}]}
  // page = a presented page index WITH a screenshot; 1..5 focuses, `at`
  // ascending, each < seconds; 0..3 captions ≤60 chars, each ≥0.5s apart
- {"type":"divider","seconds":2..5,"label":string,"roll":[string]}  // label ≤40, 1..5 roll words ≤24 each
- {"type":"reveal","seconds":2..5,"lead":string,"word":string,"sub":string}  // ≤60 / ≤24 / ≤90
- {"type":"end","seconds":2.5..6,"name":string,"tagline":string}  // ≤24 / ≤90

Binding bounds: total Σ seconds 12..90; no duplicate string within one scene;
no two scenes with identical content; no empty strings.

